#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-AD0507 expect=violation domain=ADLBC
#note "PLAN-library-template-label-resolution R2-3 (owner 2026-10-04, follow the authority): CR507 covers every variable whose name ends in DTF, so this rule judges XSDTF - the stem form label_template(\"LIBRARY\", stem=\"*DTF\") answers '{Date Imputation Flag}' for it, it is no library variable - although the longer *SDTF covers the name too and CDISC-AD0513 judges it as well. The rule keeps its authority's own test (an 'Imputation Flag' / 'Imput. Flag' ending and 'Date'): 'Start Date Imputed' has no such ending -> one violation, reported with *DTF's template. XEDTF ('End Date Imput. Flag') conforms; XDTF is the plain positive control. Under round 1 (longest-suffix governance) this rule did not judge XSDTF."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
#library variable-metadata ADLBC *DTF name=*DTF label="{Date Imputation Flag}"
#library variable-metadata ADLBC *SDTF name=*SDTF label="{Start Date Imputation Flag}"
#library variable-metadata ADLBC *EDTF name=*EDTF label="{End Date Imputation Flag}"
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt variable_name=XSDTF variable_label="Start Date Imputed" library_variable_label_template="{Date Imputation Flag}"
dataset ADLBC class=BDS
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col PARAMCD type=Char
col XDTF type=Char label="Analysis Date Imputation Flag"
col XSDTF type=Char label="Start Date Imputed"
col XEDTF type=Char label="End Date Imput. Flag"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | ALB | D | D | D
---
